  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on NRS_484B_403_3: all 10 witnesses pass and the rule composes no other rules. I used 3 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_403_3.lean`)\n- **Who it covers:** any vehicle under the `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle` definition.\n- **When it applies:** wherever the reading declares the subject's place a business district.\n- **What triggers the duty:** a U-turn is recognized (`drv_motion_u_turn`, with its three parameters) while the subject is on a highway.\n- **When the turn counts as under way:** the yaw rate's magnitude is above `p.turn_yaw_rate_tol`.\n- **How it complies:** either it is in an intersection at every under-way observation, or both of these hold:\n  - it is on a highway with a divider on it at every under-way observation;\n  - at some under-way observation it is on the divider's opening, on a highway it occupies.\n- **Narrowings:** none. I read \"on that highway\" (s6) as a highway the subject occupies, which is the record's own wording.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_403_3.lean`)\n- Each trace is 45 s at 1 s steps. The turn runs t = 30–33 s and is recognized at t = 34 s; each witness judges t = 25–44 s.\n- The heading steps through exact rational unit vectors that match the yaw rate. Run 2 failed because the heading stayed fixed while the yaw rate said it was turning.\n- The `blind` trace records the yaw rate and lets the manifest mask it.\n- The ten planned scenes reach every part of the formula, so I added no extra `branch_*` witnesses.\n\n**One thing to look at:** in run 2, `blind` was unknown because a `prim_heading_change` window was cut off by the start of the trace. That happened even at instants where the rule's own 10 s windows were fully covered. So the `drv.motion.u_turn` concept may look back further than its declared window when its inputs are unknown. More recorded history before the turn fixed it, so I filed no concept defect, but it's noted in `task_result.md`.\n\n**Process slips:**\n- I ran the gate once on the untouched skeleton, which used up a run without telling me anything new.\n- I also tried one extra shell command (the gate with `--help`). It was blocked for needing approval and didn't run; it wasn't needed.\n\nThe run-by-run log is in `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/NRS_484B_403_3/task_result.md`.",
